description:
Implement a bit selection and sign-extension module. The module takes a 32-bit input value and outputs a 32-bit value based on the value of a 3-bit function selector (funct3). It supports various operations: sign-extending the lower 8 bits when funct3 is 0, sign-extending the lower 16 bits when funct3 is 1, passing through the entire 32-bit input when funct3 is 2, zero-extending the lower 8 bits when funct3 is 4, and zero-extending the lower 16 bits when funct3 is 5. This functionality is useful for processing data in a manner consistent with some encoding or data format requirements in digital circuits.
module top_module(
    input [31:0] val_i,
    output reg [31:0] val_o,
    input [2:0] funct3
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [31:0] val_i,
    output reg [31:0] val_o,
    input [2:0] funct3
);always @*
    begin
        if(funct3 == 0) 
            val_o = { {24{val_i[7]}}, val_i[7:0] };
        else if(funct3 == 1) 
            val_o = { {16{val_i[15]}}, val_i[15:0] };
        else if(funct3 == 2) 
            val_o = val_i;
        else if(funct3 == 4) 
            val_o = { {24{1'b0}}, val_i[7:0] };
        else if(funct3 == 5) 
            val_o = { {16{1'b0}}, val_i[15:0] };
    end



endmodule

