description:
Design a simple voltage level shifter that converts a single input signal from a lower voltage level (1.8V) to a higher voltage level (3.3V). When the input signal is high (1), the output is set to the higher voltage level (3.3V); otherwise, the output is at the lower voltage level (1.8V). This module is useful for interfacing between devices operating at different voltage levels.
module top_module(
  input in,
  output out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input in,
  output out
);parameter v1 = 1.8; // voltage level of the input signal
parameter v2 = 3.3; // voltage level of the output signal

// Define the level shifting circuit using logic gates and resistors
wire intermediate_signal;
assign intermediate_signal = (in == 1'b1) ? v2 : v1;

// Connect the input signal to the level shifting circuit and the level shifting circuit to the output signal
assign out = intermediate_signal;

endmodule

