Implement the Verilog module based on the following description.
Build an 8-bit arithmetic shift register, with synchronous load. The shifter can shift both left and right, and by 1 or 2 bit positions, selected by "amount."

// Signals are defined as below:
// (1) load: Loads shift register with data[7:0] instead of shifting. Active high.
// (2) ena: Chooses whether to shift. Active high. 
// (3) amount: Chooses which direction and how much to shift. 
//     (a) 2'b00: shift left by 1 bit. 
//     (b) 2'b01: shift left by 2 bits. 
//     (c) 2'b10: shift right by 1 bit. 
//     (d) 2'b11: shift right by 2 bits. 
// (4) q: The contents of the shifter.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input load,
    input ena,
    input [1:0] amount,
    input [7:0] data,
    output reg [7:0] q);

