description:
Design a one-shot pulse generator that emits a single pulse for a configurable duration when triggered by an input signal. Upon receiving a rising edge on the trigger input, the module activates the pulse output and begins a countdown based on the specified duration, effectively translating seconds into clock cycles for a specified clock frequency (assumed to be 100 MHz). The pulse remains high during the countdown, after which it transitions low, ensuring a single output pulse that lasts for the determined period.
