description:
Design a circuit that performs a left shift operation on a 4-bit input A by 2 bits. The resulting output X, which is also 4 bits wide, is generated through specific logic gate configurations that calculate the shifted values based on the input bits. This functionality effectively discards the two least significant bits of the input while populating the two most significant bits with derived values from the remaining input bits.
